# User context: build for Vladislav

Social Agents is a personal communication-training and people-finding PWA for Vladislav Shamanov. He is 18, lives in the St. Petersburg area, and openly identifies as autistic, ADHD, and twice-exceptional (2e). Identity-first “autistic” language is welcome. Treat these as respectful identity context, not deficits or diagnoses to interpret.

## Product decisions

- Vladislav learns through mind maps and prefers minimal, direct, concrete text with clear expectations. Async interaction is fine.
- He speaks Russian, but **all UI text is simple, literal English**. Avoid idioms, euphemisms, vague hints, and unexplained social subtext.
- Keep one primary action per screen, low cognitive load, stable layouts, short steps, and calm feedback.
- Direct communication is valid. Explain implicit social meaning explicitly without teaching masking or presenting one communication style as superior.
- Support finding **adult collaborators/cofounders (18–25+)** for AI and development projects through international English-language channels such as Reddit, Telegram, Discord, meetups, and coding contests.
- Public contact only: [X @VladislavSsqwl](https://x.com/VladislavSsqwl).

## Hard privacy boundary

Never put any of the following in code, fixtures, prompts, content, documentation, screenshots, exports, or logs: email, phone number, exact address, school or university name, finances, health details beyond the labels “autistic / ADHD / 2e”, family information, secrets, or API keys.

When unsure, choose the quieter, more explicit, more private option.
